We report a moderate to strong relationship between methylation and protein differences in TI and TII myofibres, particularly in key genes/proteins involved in skeletal muscle fibre type specification. We also provide evidence that key genes/proteins involved in substrate metabolism and energy systems have higher levels of DNAm and lower levels of protein expression in TI compared to TII skeletal muscle fibres. Methylation analysis results can be found in Additional file 9.
